{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/GallerySummary.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.730Z","id":"ef1f5e8974b5ac3da5d755df4a1fb1b23f8e3f8d637f290102b2b9903b944b39","body":{"detail":"cards = questions.cards.slice(0, 2), with 'N more questions in the inbox' for the rest, as docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-06-agent-questions-and-inbox-design.md:163-165 and section 9.3 (:872-879) specify. Decision needed: keep two oldest, or show a different number or order (newest first, all of them).","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":19},"end":{"line":20},"content_hash":"c0f91b1926b1d414c397c061c7aea6ac706c4d43f2113e9bf2b678f35d0bd566"},"summary":"The gallery's unread summary shows the two oldest open questions as cards; the count is provisional","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/QuestionCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T18:49:28.381793Z","id":"66e904f14b7f78eeb3bb97f74eb4dc15da606e8dcb9e7759a87a179f5afde987","body":{"detail":"With two or more questions the primary action reads 'Answer N more' until each has an answer and, pressed early, goes to the first unanswered one. With one question there is nowhere to go and 'Answer 1 more' reads oddly, so it stays 'Answer <agent>', disabled until answered, as before. Unit test: web/shell/src/q/question-card.test.ts 'answers every kind, saying how many are left'.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":287},"end":{"line":288},"content_hash":"2ff35f5c34f6c40b2e61f656806ca83a9963cb9823d6ecaf11285c8a740a9fad"},"summary":"A card with one question keeps a disabled 'Answer <agent>' rather than saying what is left","tags":["revisit:a person reports a one-question card's disabled Answer as unclear","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/QuestionCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T18:49:28.381832Z","id":"387f99ae3b61f4f6895578ac3da41e019a64ed306cae11b70dc2140f3ddd262c","body":{"detail":"The delay lets the person see the pick land (the radio and the tab's tick) before the next question replaces the options; another pick, a tab, Back/Next or typing Other in that time cancels the move. Moving at once would be faster for a person who reads ahead; the delay runs on the shell clock (web/shell/src/clock.ts after), so the e2e tests advance it.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":50},"end":{"line":51},"content_hash":"d0a60658d61b85d04e68d716b7d2e198c67ea5ade2c4886a8010c6595c6dee4e"},"summary":"A single choice's pick moves on after 250 ms, not at once","tags":["revisit:the pause feels slow in use, or people re-pick during it","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:46:43.170210Z","id":"4ed9948843d9fa360681294ce7c64787ac2288e8ffa62a9f0e1519dfc83580d6","body":{"detail":"An approval request's card (web/shell/src/people/ApprovalCard.svelte) renders in the approver's inbox, after the questions and before the rows; the artifact view's thread card for the same thread shows no card or link to it, so a person reading the thread in the page does not see that its comments wait for their approval. The thread's withheld delivery state is the thread-card work (owner chip, withheld state) still to come.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":15},"end":{"line":20},"content_hash":"8225f923e527559eb343f82afcc389d2b57b73f994ed16227b71b7b06881eea5"},"suggested_fix":"When the thread-card work adds the withheld state, link it to /inbox?approval=<request> (the inbox focuses that card), or mount the ApprovalCard above the thread for its approver.","summary":"Approval cards show only in the inbox, not above their thread in the artifact view","tags":["task:22","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:48:04.741589Z","id":"14e1192e2c5435e56be1ac35fb88954efa3f3de8774e91304725802d22ffe23c","body":{"detail":"`load` keeps `decisions(unread).filter(i => i.read)` in the unread items, and the Read section's fetch (`readOpen ? fetch(\"read\")`) returns the same item, now read; `decided(read)` renders it again (read from the code, not reproduced in a browser), so two .acard elements carry the same data-approval and the same id `held-<request>` (the Show all button's aria-controls then names two elements, and `self()` focuses the first). Separately, after a decision `take()` replaces the item but `unread.total` keeps the old count: seen in Chromium as the header's \"2 unread\" beside \"Unread 3\".","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":110},"end":{"line":119},"content_hash":"1b081e1d4e50cfca4c569295e16d4e40c5d0d3d9b3eb016cf0ee8108fac43996"},"suggested_fix":"Leave items listed in the Unread section out of the Read section's cards, and derive the section count from the summary feed or refetch it after a decision.","summary":"A decided approval card kept in Unread also lists in an open Read section, and the Unread count goes stale after a decision","tags":["review","task:21","severity:minor","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/inbox-page.test.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:48:04.741644Z","id":"f90b151331b72ee08bc154cf25421662cd2b3e109cb4a4a26e88f432c4adebc0","body":{"detail":"The test tells the feed the decided item and checks the outcome; no `load()` runs afterwards. Deleting `...decisions(unread).filter(i => i.read),` from web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte load() leaves all 13 tests of inbox-page.test.ts passing, though a real decision is followed by an inbox event and a refetch that would drop the card from Unread.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":216},"end":{"line":225},"content_hash":"f27987f1c43583dcb17d0648af0d314e38b01ae409595547f46705485ddf3bed"},"suggested_fix":"After telling the decided item, trigger the refetch (a new-item event or the debounce) with the stub no longer listing it as unread, and check the card is still there.","summary":"The 'keeps an approval's card where it is once decided' test never refetches, so it does not test the keeping","tags":["review","task:21","severity:minor","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:48:04.741777Z","id":"c28bd93eb87858997af8a746d7d985aa3ad6bb1d0439cad64a82d6fede694684","body":{"detail":"INBOX_KINDS (web/shell/src/q/inbox-model.ts:8) is the same for every recipient; connection items go only to the owner's inbox (GET /api/inbox?kind=connection as a person answers no items), so the chip filters a person's inbox to nothing.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":250},"end":{"line":250},"content_hash":"5cb396710bc5463a5be3c873d426fa42ded5df46d45c94eca1e5e859ef23639d"},"suggested_fix":"Hide the Connections chip outside the owner's browser.","summary":"A connected person's inbox offers a Connections filter that can never match","tags":["review","task:21","severity:minor","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:16:17.631298Z","id":"25c656f1cf8fd27e1418b270bf7bc33dac039ad3db8f861313e66841e2e82eff","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a5019f38","span":{"start":{"line":110},"end":{"line":119},"content_hash":"05e108570dfc27931ada02c2c00e271aa1f49e2ff59ad0a4b4473c567d43c02d"},"summary":"The read section leaves out what Unread still shows, and take() moves the Unread and read counts when a listed item is read or unread again. Evidence: inbox-page.test.ts 'shows a decided card once when the read section, which lists it too, is open' and 'keeps an approval's card ... with the counts moved' (Unread2 to Unread1) pass; in Chromium after Decline the header says 0 unread and the section Unread 0, and with Read open the card shows once.","supersedes":"14e1192e2c5435e56be1ac35fb88954efa3f3de8774e91304725802d22ffe23c","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:16:17.633418Z","id":"9c1b6fb05291bb483c9cb238d60c3dab64bc60db493c5cf7e69b29fef336bcf6","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a5019f38","span":{"start":{"line":250},"end":{"line":250},"content_hash":"c87b0b6eca45577041b838900efb9fc8c0cf12d3b44c0a6e25123d4a33f10050"},"summary":"Only the owner's browser (the token is served) offers Connections, or a URL that already filters by it. Evidence: inbox-page.test.ts 'offers the Connections filter to the owner alone' passes; in Chromium Ivy's kinds list no Connections and the owner's do.","supersedes":"c28bd93eb87858997af8a746d7d985aa3ad6bb1d0439cad64a82d6fede694684","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/inbox-page.test.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:16:17.635375Z","id":"1084e01dce516cee62bf41b7956295198b0ffd526c65560136127e985e81a763","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a5019f38","summary":"The test now refetches with the decided item no longer listed as unread and checks the card stays. Evidence: removing the keep clause in InboxPage.load (`...decisions(unread).filter(i => i.read)`) fails it; restored, it passes.","supersedes":"f90b151331b72ee08bc154cf25421662cd2b3e109cb4a4a26e88f432c4adebc0","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:02:11.811786Z","id":"6c1452916131d7d3b3ca391c6e2e0fe6a9f2e186b7a708d7148149a8a0162535","body":{"detail":"loadStrip runs when the sections load and, debounced, on each inbox item change. An agent that starts, ends or renames without making an inbox item for this person (spec 2026-10-08 section 13: the agents topic announces those) shows in the strip only after the next inbox change or reload; block times tick on a 30 s clock.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":81},"end":{"line":81},"content_hash":"f1add4c6035f6d471f9604f2003769ef0f83030cee09058e7462a158afd034ad"},"suggested_fix":"Watch the person-scoped agents topic from the inbox page and refetch the strip on it.","summary":"The agent strip refreshes only with the inbox, not on the agents topic","tags":["task:22","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:02:11.815387Z","id":"79666c75ef479f058abf61ac3722a966f17216e5ab7d94cb8d092aba47c7e503","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:14b29df9","summary":"The artifact view puts the approver's approval card above a thread waiting for their approval (web/shell/src/ui/ShellSidebar.svelte, ThreadApproval.svelte) and the thread reads \"waiting for your approval\". Evidence: web/shell/src/thread-owner.test.ts \"puts the approver's approval card above a thread waiting for their approval\" passes; web/e2e/agent-strip.spec.ts passes (Sam allows the thread from the card above it).","supersedes":"4ed9948843d9fa360681294ce7c64787ac2288e8ffa62a9f0e1519dfc83580d6","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:22:22.164033Z","id":"1aa88592b2532bbbcada887f1ce1bbb0961b186a5015043c850c393a691a2910","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"6c1452916131d7d3b3ca391c6e2e0fe6a9f2e186b7a708d7148149a8a0162535","summary":"Assessed: a new block always comes with an inbox item (a question, or an approval request) whose event refetches the strip, so a chip saying 'waiting on you' is never missing; only an agent that starts, ends or is renamed without an item lags until the next item or reload. Low priority.","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/inbox-model.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T22:24:19.594325Z","id":"c5af8014f2df6408206e0f4390320be1d1f4e66a577d04050d309f92fcc91da5","body":{"detail":"`replier` gives replies the payload author line of spec §11 (`<name> (agent, via <harness>)`), while every other kind uses `agentLabel` (the bare name). On a single-owner install the owner's inbox reads \"web (agent, via claude) replied on Solo Page\" directly above \"web published Solo Page\"; the strip chip says \"web\" and the question card \"web in clax\". For a reader with no person, the line is \"web (The owner's agent, via claude)\" (capital T mid-phrase; same in view/sidebar-model.ts:47 and the owner chip \"web · The owner\").","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":43},"end":{"line":59},"content_hash":"b3516db5948fe65a5e36a91fa64961dedeb72487fb6eb6ad3ad97fceb7d28842"},"suggested_fix":"Use the bare name for the reader's own person's agents in the shell, and the person only for others' (as the owner chip does); lower-case an unnamed owner inside a phrase.","summary":"The owner's inbox names one agent two ways in one list: \"web (agent, via claude) replied\" beside \"web published\"","tags":["review","final-review-ui","wording","naming","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/inbox-model.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T03:13:17.315451Z","id":"072d71b0ea06a0752418f06afe4b17e4761c8ddecbb19b2df6dd3e434d6cf380","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:07908a6b","summary":"Every inbox item names its agent one way: by name, with '(Sam's agent)' when it is not the reader's own; an unnamed owner reads 'the owner' mid-sentence there, in the author line (sidebar-model.ts), the owner chip and its title (ThreadCard.svelte), the waiting label and the People panel (midName/whose in view/working-model.ts). Evidence: inbox-model.test.ts 'names an agent one way in every item...', agent-replies.spec.ts pass; Chromium: 'sam-notes (Sam's agent) replied on Quarterly Review', 'claude published Quarterly Review'.","supersedes":"c5af8014f2df6408206e0f4390320be1d1f4e66a577d04050d309f92fcc91da5","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/model.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T18:45:53.322708Z","id":"a1fc409f44eb5a8de923c9e64da97e1ef1c3bb655e996ce1dd1e296bd60491c7","body":{"detail":"Sync::question marks a copy failed both at the backoff cap and when the remote refuses it (linked_question_failed with the remote's code and message, e.g. limit_reached past 8 open copies, record c759d6e6). questionLink ignores linked.error and always says unreachable, so a refusal from a reachable remote is misnamed. Retry lives only on the Publish popover's link row (failed_questions), while a thread card's not-sent line carries its own Retry (web/shell/src/view/linked-model.ts).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":92},"end":{"line":104},"content_hash":"b93615a87f23bbdf4aefaf2ec4f77f964418693ec7bb16c6da3a82845e9a849e"},"suggested_fix":"Word a refusal from linked.error (\"Not sent: refused by <remote>\") and give the card's not-sent line the same Retry a thread card has.","summary":"A question copy the remote refused reads 'Not sent: <remote> unreachable', and its card has no Retry of its own","tags":["review","ui","status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/QuestionCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:23.225875Z","id":"aa9179ddccc301e72b141690bb9ed2b75427e8052b42a38ff3dfd8f90656d066","body":{"detail":"With two or more questions the primary action reads 'Answer N more' until each has an answer and, pressed early, goes to the first unanswered one. With one question there is nowhere to go and 'Answer 1 more' reads oddly, so it stays 'Answer <agent>', disabled until answered, as before. Unit test: web/shell/src/q/question-card.test.ts 'answers every kind, saying how many are left'.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":290},"end":{"line":291},"content_hash":"2ff35f5c34f6c40b2e61f656806ca83a9963cb9823d6ecaf11285c8a740a9fad"},"summary":"A card with one question keeps a disabled 'Answer <agent>' rather than saying what is left","supersedes":"66e904f14b7f78eeb3bb97f74eb4dc15da606e8dcb9e7759a87a179f5afde987","tags":["revisit:a person reports a one-question card's disabled Answer as unclear","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/model.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:23.239751Z","id":"5be7a536390f537cb19de7ca4ef2b1690626e538a6d168e5f5eb30ff13237edd","body":{"detail":"Sync::question marks a copy failed both at the backoff cap and when the remote refuses it (linked_question_failed with the remote's code and message, e.g. limit_reached past 8 open copies, record c759d6e6). questionLink ignores linked.error and always says unreachable, so a refusal from a reachable remote is misnamed. Retry lives only on the Publish popover's link row (failed_questions), while a thread card's not-sent line carries its own Retry (web/shell/src/view/linked-model.ts).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":93},"end":{"line":105},"content_hash":"b93615a87f23bbdf4aefaf2ec4f77f964418693ec7bb16c6da3a82845e9a849e"},"suggested_fix":"Word a refusal from linked.error (\"Not sent: refused by <remote>\") and give the card's not-sent line the same Retry a thread card has.","summary":"A question copy the remote refused reads 'Not sent: <remote> unreachable', and its card has no Retry of its own","supersedes":"a1fc409f44eb5a8de923c9e64da97e1ef1c3bb655e996ce1dd1e296bd60491c7","tags":["review","ui","status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T16:45:12.340072Z","id":"44676d5d7db98f941b12637ffdc34e9198f19047e9b955ce90c4066517375894","body":{"detail":"Moved from web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte:81, record 6c145291.\n\nloadStrip runs when the sections load and, debounced, on each inbox item change. An agent that starts, ends or renames without making an inbox item for this person (spec 2026-10-08 section 13: the agents topic announces those) shows in the strip only after the next inbox change or reload; block times tick on a 30 s clock.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":82},"end":{"line":82},"content_hash":"f1add4c6035f6d471f9604f2003769ef0f83030cee09058e7462a158afd034ad"},"suggested_fix":"Watch the person-scoped agents topic from the inbox page and refetch the strip on it.","summary":"The agent strip refreshes only with the inbox, not on the agents topic","supersedes":"6c1452916131d7d3b3ca391c6e2e0fe6a9f2e186b7a708d7148149a8a0162535","tags":["task:22","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/QuestionCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T17:46:26.995985Z","id":"0efbf2939ff72a6de8570024e0c1c8c6931aad74386458ea137596819bc00a60","body":{"detail":"Those surfaces (InboxPage.svelte:309, GallerySummary.svelte:31, extension/src/panel/InboxTab.svelte:190) render the full card through QuestionList. The card's .about link is /a/<artifact> with no ?thread=, although spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-16-ask-where-attention-is-design.md section 2 says each surface that counts a thread's question links to the thread.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":221},"end":{"line":221},"content_hash":"0520be464604e480b4694bd2ce834db62e85e1e12f02e4e3a25b74cadeac50fa"},"suggested_fix":"When q.thread?.open, link .about to /a/<artifact>?thread=<thread>.","summary":"In /inbox, the gallery's summary and the extension panel, a question asked in a thread links to its artifact, not to its thread","tags":["ui","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/TerminalCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T17:46:26.996040Z","id":"b06443230c55dc03e003441a154ed6e38a2ec9cfbb0dfc0e20fa99e5959fb12a","body":{"detail":"Each card's :global styles are injected when that card first mounts (css: injected), so a list holding only in-terminal questions would have no frame if TerminalCard relied on QuestionCard's rules. Moving the frame into QuestionList's styles would remove the copy, but it would also grow the counted question module, which is already over its budget (see the concern on web/perf/bundle-budget.json:5).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":64},"end":{"line":76},"content_hash":"9a99a564300445c0e45631e0d1a516227bbc15229ce27efaa3bb7ffe9a0d966e"},"summary":"TerminalCard repeats the .qcard frame rules under .qcard.in-terminal rather than sharing QuestionCard's","tags":["revisit:the questions bundle budget gains headroom, or the .qcard frame moves to a stylesheet every card surface loads","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/QuestionCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T18:21:19.103715Z","id":"013a5ce2579fda65999f90ffd56025e0df88b682fc4358178316b043b5a49cf7","body":{"detail":"aboutLink in web/shell/src/q/model.ts, used by QuestionCard.svelte and TerminalCard.svelte; QuestionList passes the holding thread so the link is left out inside it. Passing in just web-test at 0b7e4d15e (//web:unit 1718 passed): model.test.ts 'links a card to its thread while that is open, except inside the thread's own card'; question-card.test.ts 'links a question asked in an open thread to that thread…'; Panel.test.ts 'shows a question asked in a thread of the live page as a card, whose thread link the worker opens'.","kind":"resolve","ref":"git:1acef28e4","summary":"A card for a question in an open thread links to /a/<aid>?thread=<tid>, 'in a thread', outside that thread's own card","supersedes":"0efbf2939ff72a6de8570024e0c1c8c6931aad74386458ea137596819bc00a60","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/QuestionCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T20:21:07.820628Z","id":"9857f68a7b3776244fa9ce4d379da9e2c79c13238939b00190d894d8017b98c3","body":{"detail":"With two or more questions the primary action reads 'Answer N more' until each has an answer and, pressed early, goes to the first unanswered one. With one question there is nowhere to go and 'Answer 1 more' reads oddly, so it stays 'Answer <agent>', disabled until answered, as before. Unit test: web/shell/src/q/question-card.test.ts 'answers every kind, saying how many are left'.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":293},"end":{"line":294},"content_hash":"2ff35f5c34f6c40b2e61f656806ca83a9963cb9823d6ecaf11285c8a740a9fad"},"summary":"A card with one question keeps a disabled 'Answer <agent>' rather than saying what is left","supersedes":"aa9179ddccc301e72b141690bb9ed2b75427e8052b42a38ff3dfd8f90656d066","tags":["revisit:a person reports a one-question card's disabled Answer as unclear","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/model.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T20:21:07.843622Z","id":"eab5c36cdc99a55552a9ca9510971608355871a74d3949bb62274a224b3a1cc6","body":{"detail":"Sync::question marks a copy failed both at the backoff cap and when the remote refuses it (linked_question_failed with the remote's code and message, e.g. limit_reached past 8 open copies, record c759d6e6). questionLink ignores linked.error and always says unreachable, so a refusal from a reachable remote is misnamed. Retry lives only on the Publish popover's link row (failed_questions), while a thread card's not-sent line carries its own Retry (web/shell/src/view/linked-model.ts).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":107},"end":{"line":119},"content_hash":"b93615a87f23bbdf4aefaf2ec4f77f964418693ec7bb16c6da3a82845e9a849e"},"suggested_fix":"Word a refusal from linked.error (\"Not sent: refused by <remote>\") and give the card's not-sent line the same Retry a thread card has.","summary":"A question copy the remote refused reads 'Not sent: <remote> unreachable', and its card has no Retry of its own","supersedes":"5be7a536390f537cb19de7ca4ef2b1690626e538a6d168e5f5eb30ff13237edd","tags":["review","ui","status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/TerminalCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T20:21:08.025546Z","id":"76d8f8da7af29a81e926e552fb6c18d4a854e04d9517ea5ad87a34ad8cb32f5d","body":{"detail":"Each card's :global styles are injected when that card first mounts (css: injected), so a list holding only in-terminal questions would have no frame if TerminalCard relied on QuestionCard's rules. Moving the frame into QuestionList's styles would remove the copy, but it would also grow the counted question module, which is already over its budget (see the concern on web/perf/bundle-budget.json:5).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":72},"end":{"line":88},"content_hash":"7c76f1b97257d85bd41f0d74d40ace8e594fa57af269108370cb91ab283919cb"},"summary":"TerminalCard repeats the .qcard frame rules under .qcard.in-terminal rather than sharing QuestionCard's","supersedes":"b06443230c55dc03e003441a154ed6e38a2ec9cfbb0dfc0e20fa99e5959fb12a","tags":["revisit:the questions bundle budget gains headroom, or the .qcard frame moves to a stylesheet every card surface loads","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/model.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T20:27:22.434966Z","id":"19410260f302c9c8d4a2ac58baa321f88468d2aabe026bee777762d07f5c7e92","body":{"detail":"inThread reads q.thread.open from the question view, which the daemon computes when the view is read. Resolving the thread (POST /api/artifacts/{aid}/threads/{tid}/resolve, crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs:1480) sends no change on the questions topic, and QuestionFeed (web/shell/src/q/feed.svelte.ts) fetches only on ready or resync. An open page therefore keeps the question in the resolved thread's card, and the sidebar keeps its link, rather than moving it to the sidebar's block as a card. After a reload the card is in the block: web/e2e/ask-where.spec.ts, \"a resolved thread's question moves to the sidebar's block as a card\", reloads before checking. Without the reload, the card did not appear in .side-q within 5 s.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":78},"end":{"line":81},"content_hash":"dc28c8aa67cac9d60348c3508d98398dd301e11a29fd2277b654e2eca9ad08cb"},"suggested_fix":"Have resolve, reopen and delete of a thread publish a question change for each open question asked in it, or have the question module re-fetch when the view's thread list changes a thread's status.","summary":"A thread question stays in its thread card after the thread resolves, until the questions are fetched again","tags":["ui","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/TerminalCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T21:06:54.307787Z","id":"82ff9171c2b66ec464849aa891357eecb3404ee53626552646c1572079886668","body":{"detail":"Each card's :global styles are injected when that card first mounts (css: injected), so a list holding only in-terminal questions would have no frame if TerminalCard relied on QuestionCard's rules. Moving the frame into QuestionList's styles would remove the copy, but it would also grow the counted question module, which is already over its budget (see the concern on web/perf/bundle-budget.json:5).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":73},"end":{"line":89},"content_hash":"c3d3a10e7600a4303c6c6c4dc0337889cfaa57d8ec1d8412db79c8970b7a17fd"},"summary":"TerminalCard repeats the .qcard frame rules under .qcard.in-terminal rather than sharing QuestionCard's","supersedes":"76d8f8da7af29a81e926e552fb6c18d4a854e04d9517ea5ad87a34ad8cb32f5d","tags":["revisit:the questions bundle budget gains headroom, or the .qcard frame moves to a stylesheet every card surface loads","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/model.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T21:06:54.330596Z","id":"39d62050ee9d45e667a05e4d39a57a9858a764f6d7fc8081fca0a38d3e383c78","body":{"detail":"Sync::question marks a copy failed both at the backoff cap and when the remote refuses it (linked_question_failed with the remote's code and message, e.g. limit_reached past 8 open copies, record c759d6e6). questionLink ignores linked.error and always says unreachable, so a refusal from a reachable remote is misnamed. Retry lives only on the Publish popover's link row (failed_questions), while a thread card's not-sent line carries its own Retry (web/shell/src/view/linked-model.ts).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":108},"end":{"line":120},"content_hash":"b93615a87f23bbdf4aefaf2ec4f77f964418693ec7bb16c6da3a82845e9a849e"},"suggested_fix":"Word a refusal from linked.error (\"Not sent: refused by <remote>\") and give the card's not-sent line the same Retry a thread card has.","summary":"A question copy the remote refused reads 'Not sent: <remote> unreachable', and its card has no Retry of its own","supersedes":"eab5c36cdc99a55552a9ca9510971608355871a74d3949bb62274a224b3a1cc6","tags":["review","ui","status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/model.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T21:07:10.010125Z","id":"9893f953b1028217e0c1cd52e973b85bf2af365b4d7a312b988d1c5057d24ef7","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:356317448","summary":"Fixed: resolve, reopen and delete of a thread now publish each open question asked in it again (clax_http::views::question::announce_thread, called from crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs resolve, reopen and delete), so the open page upserts the view with its new thread.open and moves the card. Evidence: bazelisk test //crates/clax-server:all --test_arg=api_where_to_ask passed, including api_where_to_ask::resolving_reopening_or_deleting_a_thread_announces_its_open_questions; bazelisk test //web:e2e_rest --test_arg=--grep=ask-where.spec: 24 passed, with \"a resolved thread's question moves to the sidebar's block as a card\" (web/e2e/ask-where.spec.ts) now checking the move without a reload.","supersedes":"19410260f302c9c8d4a2ac58baa321f88468d2aabe026bee777762d07f5c7e92","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/feed.svelte.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T22:37:58.107526Z","id":"217cd397aaee94c94aa6c75a25404451582c7cb7d92754e8c0d57ccd84163454","body":{"detail":"InboxFeed.on (web/shell/src/q/feed.svelte.ts:281) sets `unread` from every event, and `summary()` sets it again from a GET started at `ready`, `resync`, `inbox_read` or SUMMARY_MS after an item change. A summary the daemon read before an item was made, whose answer lands after that item's event, puts the older count back until the next event or summary. QuestionFeed.refetch had the same shape and now replays the events heard while it was in flight; the inbox has no per-item list to replay into, so a fix needs the summary to carry a sequence (the inbox's newest `seq`) that the feed compares with the events'.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":233},"end":{"line":241},"content_hash":"e9e100bb7aedbf5ae9466ea2dfaa4dba4b2bedbda2c8d07085e99c7cf1dcb947"},"suggested_fix":"Return the newest inbox seq with the summary and with each event's unread, and keep the count from whichever is newer.","summary":"A summary read before an inbox event can overwrite the newer unread count that event carried","tags":["race","shell","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/QuestionList.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T22:37:58.108398Z","id":"7f0b4eb8c6cb2283501ee93e03e426701cdf48be81e5dc003f900ac22409578e","body":{"detail":"`need()` (web/shell/src/q/later.svelte.ts:10) resets its promise on a failed import, but this effect, and the one at web/shell/src/q/SidebarQuestions.svelte:25, reruns only when its list changes. A chunk that fails to load once (a daemon restarting under the page) leaves an in-terminal question with no terminal card until another question arrives or closes. index.ts `check` has the same shape for the thread slots.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":37},"end":{"line":37},"content_hash":"f0302c7b68a424806e4e38a1295298b3c035229a54ad9540293aa8e5889c95eb"},"suggested_fix":"Retry `need()` on the stream's `stream_up`/`ready`, or have `need()` retry with a backoff while a caller waits.","summary":"A failed load of the on-demand parts is tried again only when the list changes","tags":["shell","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/QuestionCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T20:00:51.122459Z","id":"cf4b7d1f1dbedc1a59d4bbbe7390d3119013c61b0414e34b12fa5a5955aa30ff","body":{"detail":"The delay lets the person see the pick land (the radio and the tab's tick) before the next question replaces the options; another pick, a tab, Back/Next or typing Other in that time cancels the move. Moving at once would be faster for a person who reads ahead; the delay runs on the shell clock (web/shell/src/clock.ts after), so the e2e tests advance it.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":52},"end":{"line":53},"content_hash":"d0a60658d61b85d04e68d716b7d2e198c67ea5ade2c4886a8010c6595c6dee4e"},"summary":"A single choice's pick moves on after 250 ms, not at once","supersedes":"387f99ae3b61f4f6895578ac3da41e019a64ed306cae11b70dc2140f3ddd262c","tags":["revisit:the pause feels slow in use, or people re-pick during it","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/QuestionCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T22:50:26.294421Z","id":"2ec9a6533f0312fe306e4e5b55aef3ad1ab0d8fc98470f875655d4a0aeef4ddc","body":{"detail":"showQuestions (web/shell/src/app/host.ts:472) focuses the .qcard by script with no prior pointer input in the shell, so Chromium matches :focus-visible and this rule draws a 2px --focus outline around the card, inside the sheet's own green top border (seen at 390x800: computed outline-style solid, :focus-visible true). In the app the sheet usually opens by itself on a new question, so the ring shows every time. An app-mode rule such as html.app .app-questions .qcard:focus-visible { outline: none } (the card's controls keep their own rings) would keep keyboard focus on the card without the ring.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":305},"end":{"line":305},"content_hash":"bdbed80e147140ad5b5cde99eb105aa7ea1da7af5fbf8f7b1fed500c3fc7177f"},"summary":"openQuestions() draws the keyboard focus ring around the whole card in the app's sheet","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/feed.svelte.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T22:50:26.294471Z","id":"be6eab1872695817e42104ed434d45b76011828dc8437c831f3ff4fe14faf1f6","body":{"detail":"Before 647958f22844 the open list shrank first (a listener saw the card in neither list, so q/index.ts told {open: 0, shown: 0} and the host closed the sheet), then recent grew. surfaces.test.ts checks only counts.at(-1) after the answer, which is {open: 0, shown: 1} under either order, and feed.test.ts has no listener assertion for it. A feed test that records byArtifact() at every listener call during upsert of a closed question, and asserts the card is in one of the lists each time, would catch the order coming back.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":115},"end":{"line":117},"content_hash":"2284d0660465ac1f87c6e07c47b2695bb8e9901e3e16e4fb37c19cc4689bd4bb"},"summary":"No test pins the closing question's single change, which keeps the app's sheet open on an answer","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/feed.svelte.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T22:55:45.415691Z","id":"948fac8de83fbe5f48fccd10465e3186f864bda719f9954f39f61c49cbae384f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Pinned in 647958f22844: feed.test.ts 'tells a question closing as one change: every listener sees its card, open or closed' records open and recent at each listener call. With feed.svelte.ts from 647958f22844~1 it fails (expected [ { open: [], recent: [] }, …(1) ] to deeply equal [ { open: [], recent: [ 'Q1' ] } ]); with the current order it passes.","supersedes":"be6eab1872695817e42104ed434d45b76011828dc8437c831f3ff4fe14faf1f6","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/QuestionCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T22:55:45.416304Z","id":"ef5e52a844e81b2b479bb46d31d963487464806a1ad90ef96074077590eb230b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Fixed in 647958f22844 with an app-mode rule in web/shell/src/app/app.css (html.app .app-questions .qcard:focus-visible { outline: none }); the card's controls keep their rings. Chromium 390x800, card focused by openQuestions: :focus-visible true, computed outline-style none.","supersedes":"2ec9a6533f0312fe306e4e5b55aef3ad1ab0d8fc98470f875655d4a0aeef4ddc","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/index.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T05:22:16.373859Z","id":"3320be6909bd039b29008c3846f25f69bd9c81f7c7f573eb6ead35d10df292d1","body":{"detail":"artifact() mounts SidebarQuestions into the app's sheet (.app-questions > .questions-slot, slot() at line 100) instead of the hidden sidebar, but SidebarQuestions (web/shell/src/q/SidebarQuestions.svelte:19-30) shows only the questions in no thread as cards; a question in an open thread (inThread) appears there only as a ThreadLinks link (?thread=<id>) and counts in the heading, while its card, with the answer controls, is mounted by followSlots (line 125) into the thread card's .thread-q-slot in the sidebar, which app mode hides. The app is also told the question is open (count(), clax-questions), so its badge and openQuestions() lead to a sheet with nothing to answer. This came from merging main's thread-card questions (a9c3a79a3c0b, 52d65826a74c) with the branch's app-mode sheet (647958f22844). Options: show thread questions as cards in the sheet in app mode (pass a flag to SidebarQuestions), or have the app's thread view mount the thread's .thread-q-slot.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":100},"end":{"line":126},"content_hash":"3af76e9e5f475d487953cfb5d96d13246cc938618fb51b407c252eec66c27031"},"summary":"In app mode a question placed in a thread can be answered only in that thread's card, inside the hidden sidebar","tags":["app-mode","questions","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/index.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T05:22:33.607982Z","id":"3e70286ad9abb42a2178771aeb8fd02bdbb2694016841391a8ec0d825eaa88db","body":{"detail":"artifact() mounts SidebarQuestions into the app's sheet (.app-questions > .questions-slot, slot() at line 100) instead of the hidden sidebar, but SidebarQuestions (web/shell/src/q/SidebarQuestions.svelte:19-30) shows only the questions in no thread as cards; a question in an open thread (inThread) appears there only as a ThreadLinks link (?thread=<id>) and counts in the heading, while its card, with the answer controls, is mounted by followSlots (line 125) into the thread card's .thread-q-slot in the sidebar, which app mode hides. The app is also told the question is open (count(), clax-questions), so its badge and openQuestions() lead to a sheet with nothing to answer. It comes from joining main's thread-card questions (a9c3a79a3c0b, 52d65826a74c) with the app-mode sheet (the commit 'Dock the shell's question card in app mode and tell the app how many questions are open'). Options: show thread questions as cards in the sheet in app mode (a flag to SidebarQuestions), or have the app's thread view mount the thread's .thread-q-slot.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":100},"end":{"line":126},"content_hash":"3af76e9e5f475d487953cfb5d96d13246cc938618fb51b407c252eec66c27031"},"summary":"In app mode a question placed in a thread can be answered only in that thread's card, inside the hidden sidebar","supersedes":"3320be6909bd039b29008c3846f25f69bd9c81f7c7f573eb6ead35d10df292d1","tags":["app-mode","questions","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/inbox-groups.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:05:25.579623Z","id":"af558a4d1d570e730e07cce1a5a63eeda88d8a3a4598dd8a5ffb79197f9575e1","body":{"detail":"Connection requests, machines that connected by invite, ended agents and questions asked outside a page have no artifact_id. They go in one group keyed `none` (the `artifact=none` filter of GET /api/inbox, crates/clax-server/src/routes/inbox.rs NO_ARTIFACT), ordered by its newest item like any page's group, titled \"Other\" with no link. A group per agent was considered: it would need a second grouping key in the store's GROUP BY (crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs Shape::Groups) and a way to page an agent's artifact-less items, and the agent strip already filters by agent. Connection requests, the most common of these items, are cards above the groups anyway.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":9},"end":{"line":30},"content_hash":"c324ce319ce1438ef23b73af2b9eec8707803a81fd56e7dd334440a866e144a4"},"summary":"Items about no artifact share one group, \"Other\", rather than a group per agent","tags":["inbox","shell","revisit:the Other group regularly holds more than a screenful of items from several agents","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/GallerySummary.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:05:25.579945Z","id":"a0559b4941cc1a9cd1bb66bd34e3fea39d4e716e425857dcf96d8a144a66cd6f","body":{"detail":"The summary shows at most five rows above the gallery and links to /inbox for the rest; headings per page would take more room than the rows they group, and the gallery's cards already sit by artifact. /inbox groups (web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":21},"end":{"line":21},"content_hash":"c4868a407aad28fe73f911729fb2e958c0ce4c2928b5ca701165913c89b4d2ad"},"summary":"The gallery's unread summary keeps its five newest unread rows flat, not grouped by artifact","tags":["inbox","shell","revisit:the summary shows more than five rows","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:05:25.580407Z","id":"18d423034144112c25262b6fddc4bf9a46fd2884c05c437305f2f7160cb1b01d","body":{"detail":"The page fetches the unread question, approval and connection items (MAX_CARDS = 200) separately from the groups, and a group's rows and new count leave out exactly the items shown as cards. With more than 200 such items unread, the older ones are not cards: they show as rows in their page's group and count as new there. Before grouping, the flat unread list showed only its first page's cards too.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":145},"end":{"line":155},"content_hash":"12cd71622e0f6356e3d4b0842310ee9baa9c1484b99578c59ed206c9109bbae1"},"summary":"Only the 200 newest unread card items show as cards; older open questions and requests fall into their groups as rows","tags":["inbox","shell","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:05:25.580523Z","id":"79da425d8bddee6738065b758a3c54de9f23a020891a3532330b19e0766026e0","body":{"detail":"The two sections stay as before grouping: Unread groups the unread items by page (each group open while it has something new), Read groups the read ones behind its count (groups folded unless there is one). A single list of every page, those with nothing new folded beside the rest, was the other reading of the collapsible-groups design; it would merge the sections and their counts. Kept the sections pending the owner's call.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":117},"end":{"line":117},"content_hash":"27dda22ed2dc4f7548af947836ebbcfa3feb4dae80b6ed22338b90277c3b8752"},"summary":"Unread lists only pages with something unread; a page with nothing new shows in the folded Read section alone","tags":["inbox","shell","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:23:32.339125Z","id":"33bba728892898462d0b83b8c7dc20579979069e3fd13ee9c6d0a2346aa1661a","body":{"detail":"Failure: a group lists its 3 newest unread rows of 5 unread; the 4th is read from another tab or a notification. take() computes the count change only from an item it already lists (`was`, line 308, from cardItems or the groups' items), so d = 0; takeItem (web/shell/src/q/inbox-groups.ts:56) then leaves the group's unread at 5, and since the item is read, line 315 does not call soon() either. The header keeps saying \"5 new\", Mark read stays offered and the Unread section total stays one high until the next full load. takeItem's doc comment says the count moves \"whether listed or not\", but the caller never passes a delta for an unlisted item. The unit test at web/shell/src/q/inbox-page.test.ts:143 covers only a listed row.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":303},"end":{"line":316},"content_hash":"04300d04e095affb193a0b610c14c95263d523f6843080f1997968489aa01dcd"},"suggested_fix":"For an item not listed in the unread section, refetch (soon()) when its read state changes and its group is shown, or have the stream event carry the previous read state so the delta can be applied to its group by groupKey.","summary":"A group's new count and Mark read go stale when an item past its listed rows is read elsewhere","tags":["review","review:inbox-by-artifact","inbox","shell","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:23:32.339433Z","id":"a1812d93119c14344614796c11fb67902a36dc11b8d58ae9d1a80e4f733fd238","body":{"detail":"Failure: page P has one open question (a pinned card above the groups) and two unread replies; its group says \"2 new\" (freshOf, line 118, leaves card items out). Clicking the group's Mark read posts {all: true, filter: {artifact: P}, upto} (markGroup, line 284); the store's mark-all (crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs build, Shape::MarkAll) excludes only undecided approvals, so the question's item is marked read too. load() then refetches the cards with read=unread and keeps only cards whose question is no longer open, so the still-open question's card disappears from the pinned list although the group never counted or showed it. The server's `marked` is 3 where the header said 2.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":271},"end":{"line":284},"content_hash":"5535712c16cb76acfd6a74be4cea062b1d98b4a40db2322a328b3a6fde76431e"},"suggested_fix":"Send the group's mark with the kinds it shows as rows (the filter's kinds minus question, approval and connection), or mark the IDs the group lists plus a server filter that excludes open question items.","summary":"A group's Mark read also reads the open questions about that page, dropping their pinned cards","tags":["review","review:inbox-by-artifact","inbox","shell","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/InboxGroup.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:23:32.343675Z","id":"1dce142a62636574a4012f6c64a2f428508499698b53af59a2d660adfef19db4","body":{"detail":"The group title sits in a div with a button, not an h-element, so screen-reader heading navigation (the page has h2 Inbox, h3 sections, h4 for the pinned cards) cannot move between groups. Each <section aria-label={title}> is a region landmark, so a page of 20 groups adds 20 landmarks to the landmark list. The toggle carries aria-expanded and also changes its accessible name (\"Show X\" / \"Hide X\"), so it announces e.g. \"Hide Board, expanded\"; the WAI-ARIA disclosure pattern keeps the name fixed and lets aria-expanded carry the state (https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/patterns/disclosure/). aria-controls names the body's ID, which is only rendered while open.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":61},"end":{"line":71},"content_hash":"f89a3695a8c74eb1f26387a9c7f2a0f79847a42d81da43fa9898e66fedebd021"},"suggested_fix":"Wrap the toggle button in an h4 (name: the title), drop aria-label from the section (or use a plain div), give the toggle a fixed label, and keep the body element rendered with hidden while folded.","summary":"A group's header is not a heading, every group is a named region, and the toggle's label flips with its state","tags":["review","review:inbox-by-artifact","inbox","a11y","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:26:04.629698Z","id":"cf9e160f6e751c80589cd224d29dc43c8da218a7fee0b01935ffa3ba2a20ec37","body":{"detail":"web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte:308 finds `was` only in cardItems or the listed group items; for an unlisted item it is undefined, so line 309 gives d = 0 and line 314 calls takeItem(unread.groups, item, 0) (web/shell/src/q/inbox-groups.ts:59-66 then leaves g.unread unchanged). Line 316 calls soon() only when `!item.read`, so a read item never refetches. The group's unread, freshOf (line 118), the \"N new\" header and the Mark read button (onRead gated on fresh) stay stale until the next load().","kind":"comment","references":"33bba728892898462d0b83b8c7dc20579979069e3fd13ee9c6d0a2346aa1661a","summary":"confirmed: an unlisted item read elsewhere leaves its group's unread count unchanged and triggers no refetch","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:26:04.629915Z","id":"f5a3cb6b0d955fca4251d6d0b83561bc32dfac26065bb13e535f5894a84582f7","body":{"detail":"markGroup (web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte:284) sends {...filter, artifact: g.key} with upto = newestSeq(g.items); with no kind filter, the store's mark-all (crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs:387-410, Shape::MarkAll) excludes only undecided approvals (UNDECIDED, lines 634-640), not questions. Question items carry the asking artifact (note_question, inbox.rs:1278 artifact_id: q.artifact_id). After the mark, load() (InboxPage.svelte:173-181) refetches cards with read=unread (fetchCards, line 154) and keeps from the previous cards only those with status !== \"open\" (line 178), so an open question's card disappears. freshOf (line 118) subtracts card items from the group's count, so the button's count never included it. Applies when the question's seq is at or below the group's newest listed seq.","kind":"comment","references":"a1812d93119c14344614796c11fb67902a36dc11b8d58ae9d1a80e4f733fd238","summary":"confirmed: a group's Mark read also marks open question items about that page, and their pinned cards drop out","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/InboxGroup.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:26:04.630259Z","id":"c93e039b42a2803ebf88e3088eaea3043dad288a7b38874c63f37513ff6f7714","body":{"detail":"The markup is at web/shell/src/q/InboxGroup.svelte:36-52 (the finding's span 61-71 now covers its CSS): line 36 <section ... aria-label={title}> (a named region landmark); line 39 the header is a <div class=\"ghead\">, no h-element; line 40 the toggle has aria-expanded={p.open} and aria-label={`${p.open ? \"Hide\" : \"Show\"} ${title}`}; aria-controls={p.id} names the body rendered only inside {#if p.open} (lines 47-48). InboxPage.svelte has h2 (line 348), h3 (line 386) and an h4 for the pinned cards' heading (line 390). The disclosure pattern at https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/patterns/disclosure/ conveys state with aria-expanded.","kind":"comment","references":"1dce142a62636574a4012f6c64a2f428508499698b53af59a2d660adfef19db4","summary":"confirmed: no heading element, a named section per group, a state-flipping toggle label, aria-controls to an unrendered ID","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:21:40.584669Z","id":"9431a0f0a1a8d8c51d640402d8817202b20a9c0e89f53657b594b8d0db3d1930","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:119ab1197","summary":"Fixed: a group's Mark read sends except with its page's unread items shown as cards, and mark-all leaves them unread. Evidence: inbox-page.test.ts 'marks a group read but its page's question pinned as a card, which it does not count' (body except [IQ]), the store's mark_all_leaves_the_items_it_is_told_to_except, and api_inbox::group_by_artifact_counts_every_match_and_pages_each_group (marked 1, the question stays unread) pass under Bazel.","supersedes":"a1812d93119c14344614796c11fb67902a36dc11b8d58ae9d1a80e4f733fd238","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:21:40.642597Z","id":"8cdb6f5c8d2856b6ba8d66d43da92f1057dd43948ff4df66b7c8ac30c906c7ff","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:9c595fe50","summary":"Fixed: take() fetches the sections again when an item not listed changes while its group is shown, and takeItem's doc says which deltas its callers pass. Evidence: inbox-page.test.ts 'fetches the groups again when an item of a shown group, past its listed rows, is read elsewhere' (5 new to 4 new) passes in //web:unit.","supersedes":"33bba728892898462d0b83b8c7dc20579979069e3fd13ee9c6d0a2346aa1661a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/InboxGroup.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:21:40.894977Z","id":"925ad65056f4f62208a5f05cf06b07bdea3076d271b1fd620574656241642819","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:dec2460dc","summary":"Fixed: the group is a plain div, its title an h4, its toggle named by the heading (aria-labelledby) with the state in aria-expanded alone, and its body always rendered, hidden while folded. Evidence: inbox-page.test.ts checks aria-labelledby, aria-controls resolving to the body, no named section and the hidden body; e2e/inbox.spec.ts drives the toggle by its fixed name and aria-expanded; both pass.","supersedes":"1dce142a62636574a4012f6c64a2f428508499698b53af59a2d660adfef19db4","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/QuestionCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:19:43.040212Z","id":"f3dc5cc209ccb40a6196a80f5cf7dbc2bb845556d15b019eeb77e8e500e7819f","body":{"detail":"Only comment and reply bodies render as Markdown (docs/contract.md, Comments and feedback). A question's preview is shown in a <pre> as a monospace mock-up, which Markdown rendering would reflow; its question and option text are agent-written and may hold Markdown syntax that shows literally. Rendering them would reuse ui/Markdown.svelte; whether to is the owner's call.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":275},"end":{"line":275},"content_hash":"f1ffc4e5e38b6baeca010bd353831878d10948a91731da29f5fa07c4922403e5"},"summary":"An agent's question text, option descriptions and option previews stay plain text, not Markdown","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:09:29.707936Z","id":"4959a906562618c3b128c424c81fadf59fdc4432379b7693f9cdd552c7ba9a24","body":{"detail":"Moved from web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte:81, record 6c145291.\n\nloadStrip runs when the sections load and, debounced, on each inbox item change. An agent that starts, ends or renames without making an inbox item for this person (spec 2026-10-08 section 13: the agents topic announces those) shows in the strip only after the next inbox change or reload; block times tick on a 30 s clock.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":101},"end":{"line":101},"content_hash":"f1add4c6035f6d471f9604f2003769ef0f83030cee09058e7462a158afd034ad"},"suggested_fix":"Watch the person-scoped agents topic from the inbox page and refetch the strip on it.","summary":"The agent strip refreshes only with the inbox, not on the agents topic","supersedes":"44676d5d7db98f941b12637ffdc34e9198f19047e9b955ce90c4066517375894","tags":["task:22","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/QuestionCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T00:04:26.775589Z","id":"3262cbf6d6bed7be97d0df684eebcabe725b90ca39be0e7c1cad24ce871ea548","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7091a44bd","summary":"A question's text renders through ui/Markdown.svelte, open (.qtext) and closed (.answers .q); previews stay verbatim in their <pre>, and inbox rows and notifications show the text through plainText. Tests: web/shell/src/q/question-card.test.ts 'question text as Markdown', web/shell/src/view/markdown.test.ts 'is what the inbox's one-line text shows for an unanswered question', web/e2e/questions.spec.ts 'an agent's question renders as Markdown in its card' (bazelisk test //web:unit and //web:e2e_rest --test_arg=--grep=..., both pass). Option descriptions stay text: see the alternative on line 267.","supersedes":"f3dc5cc209ccb40a6196a80f5cf7dbc2bb845556d15b019eeb77e8e500e7819f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/QuestionCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T00:04:26.825083Z","id":"96ef3e452ce200a2ce8bd6b4a4c324ba72ee0cb063a47b470da4bea79e053571","body":{"detail":"Only a question's text renders as Markdown; an option's label and description are text, as docs/contract.md's question shape says. A description sits inside the option's <label>, so a link in it would compete with picking the option, and it is part of the option's accessible name.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":267},"end":{"line":267},"content_hash":"6bf1150623a7bfb11e27dd83fe436fceefbed34c3def242643d8aa4e1c6b05e1"},"summary":"Render an option's description as Markdown too","tags":["revisit:agents write Markdown syntax in option descriptions that shows literally","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T00:03:20.169013Z","id":"73e0da2689f747173e45557736b035d095bdf35e0858051331d7e2e45989a465","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:6ff52581f","summary":"Owner's decision: one list. Each page appears once as a group, newest group first; a group with something new is bold, says how many and starts open on its new items then its recent read ones; one with nothing new is a quiet folded line; an Unread chip narrows the list; the Read section is gone. Built in 1cf7071ce (group rows unread first, then read, with u/r cursors) and 6ff52581f. Evidence: e2e/inbox.spec.ts 'lists each page once: new ones open and bold, the rest folded, the Unread chip, a group's Mark read in place, the Page filter' passes, with inbox-page.test.ts (53 inbox tests in //web:unit) and api_inbox::group_by_artifact_counts_every_match_and_pages_each_group.","supersedes":"79da425d8bddee6738065b758a3c54de9f23a020891a3532330b19e0766026e0","tags":["reason:fixed","status:decided","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T00:03:32.512377Z","id":"a7d1a3455962b3c60a4c131c4cb7e8ffb317c89d84fcaa3f8370508afdcd59b6","body":{"detail":"The page fetches the unread question, approval and connection items (MAX_CARDS = 200) separately from the groups, and a group's rows and new count leave out exactly the items shown as cards. With more than 200 such items unread, the older ones are not cards: they show as rows in their page's group and count as new there. Before grouping, the flat unread list showed only its first page's cards too.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":145},"end":{"line":152},"content_hash":"c7fec710e98462a578cc37bea255eebdca8bd863e61a1ae640a8680238e30ace"},"summary":"Only the 200 newest unread card items show as cards; older open questions and requests fall into their groups as rows","supersedes":"18d423034144112c25262b6fddc4bf9a46fd2884c05c437305f2f7160cb1b01d","tags":["inbox","shell","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T00:08:23.746751Z","id":"cb7873e276ea46cc594df7adc937b0e7a78e3cf233b0aad5f1354024d16083d0","body":{"detail":"Failure: with more than 20 groups (DEFAULT_GROUPS, crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs:34), click More pages, then Mark read on a group from the second page: markUpTo (InboxPage.svelte:253-263) calls load(), which fetches only the first page of groups and replaces the list (`list = l`, InboxPage.svelte:174), so that group and the whole second page vanish and the page jumps. Likewise a group expanded by Show more (say 23 rows) falls back to its 3 first rows. The same load() runs on every new unread item and on an unlisted item read elsewhere (soon(), InboxPage.svelte:284 and 299), so either also collapses the paged list. The header comment (InboxPage.svelte:18-19) and docs promise a group keeps its place on Mark read. No test covers Mark read or a refetch after More pages or Show more (inbox-page.test.ts 'marks one group read ...' lists one page of three rows).","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":251},"end":{"line":263},"content_hash":"c7674d9b62509952c7e95f75133a5ac7c2a91dfa9aaa8e179c4616b58b65677f"},"suggested_fix":"On a mark or refetch, refetch as many groups as are listed (limit = groups shown, or page up to the old last cursor) and keep each group's listed row count (rows = its listed rows, up to MAX_GROUP_ROWS, then append), or update the marked group in place (its items read, unread 0) without a full reload; add a unit test that Mark read on a second-page group keeps it and its rows.","summary":"A group's Mark read (and any live refetch) drops the groups listed by More pages and the rows added by Show more","tags":["review","review:inbox-one-list","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T00:08:23.746988Z","id":"435215598d6af7f50473d74747b527a140e69b4e80cdd00747c24b520974b3de","body":{"detail":"With filter.read 'unread' (InboxPage.svelte:248) the groups fetch asks read=unread; markGroup's load() refetches, and the just-read group no longer matches, so it disappears and every group below moves up. A live read elsewhere keeps it (as a quiet line) until the next refetch, then it disappears too. Whether the Unread view should keep a just-read group in place (as the default view does) is the owner's call.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":264},"end":{"line":268},"content_hash":"afca8003331c32a5589cf8c9bcef65166960319216c94d8736c7c614e6290d95"},"suggested_fix":"Either keep groups listed for this search across a refetch (drop them only on a new search), or accept removal under the Unread chip and say so in the page's header comment and docs.","summary":"With the Unread chip on, a group's Mark read removes that group and the list below it jumps up","tags":["review","review:inbox-one-list","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/InboxGroup.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T00:08:23.747023Z","id":"d15d01eec0c30b75f38307a100aeb9c2ce7f7d73c605aab655200c042c081741","body":{"detail":"The toggle is named by the h3 title only (aria-labelledby, InboxGroup.svelte:42) and 'N new' sits in .gmeta after the heading (line 46). With the Unread/Read sections gone, bold weight (data-fresh, line 67) is the only other distinction, which is visual. A screen-reader user moving by headings (h3) or buttons hears every group alike and must read each line to find the ones with something new.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":42},"end":{"line":46},"content_hash":"e220bcad82c20d97dd1c0fc7463f52d747a85373f365bc5b91e0ca2e27aa8ae5"},"suggested_fix":"Put the count in the heading (a visually styled span inside the h3) or add aria-describedby on the toggle pointing at the .gnew span.","summary":"A group's 'N new' is outside its heading and toggle name, so heading or button navigation cannot tell new groups from quiet ones","tags":["review","review:inbox-one-list","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T00:08:23.747241Z","id":"915e999fcbf2d3b5a9bf324ac3021430acf018fa027fc0d26f2697f10399fdec","body":{"detail":"The Unread chip is inside .filters (InboxPage.svelte:345-346), which at max-width 700px is display:none until Filters is pressed (line 416). The one list's main narrowing control is thus two taps away on a phone, and whether it is on is not visible while the filters are closed.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":345},"end":{"line":346},"content_hash":"5f65c96e23bf7d291d3b59c71a2e2e89b69191d9daa61d836147546284a14fb6"},"suggested_fix":"Place the Unread chip in .find beside the search box (or show it outside .filters at phone width).","summary":"At phone width the Unread chip is hidden behind Filters","tags":["review","review:inbox-one-list","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/InboxGroup.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T00:10:19.183233Z","id":"5d1ee9c347db20f563cd973800174df13bd04f53e81c7529b320ff40d3f27cab","body":{"detail":"web/shell/src/q/InboxGroup.svelte:42 sets aria-labelledby={`${p.id}-t`} on .gtoggle, pointing at the h3 (:45) that holds only the title; the 'N new' span (.gnew) is in .gmeta at :46, a sibling after the heading, with no aria-describedby linking it. The only other per-group difference is styling ([data-fresh] at :38 and the font-weight rule in the style block) and the presence of the Mark read button (InboxPage.svelte:324 passes onRead only when fresh), which heading navigation does not reach. Concern is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"d15d01eec0c30b75f38307a100aeb9c2ce7f7d73c605aab655200c042c081741","summary":"confirmed: the toggle is named by the h3 only and 'N new' sits outside it","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T00:10:19.183396Z","id":"e4713a05323ad0d1e6d11d9d8df4ed877125674de2ef32222c3b133c79f4f5ee","body":{"detail":"markUpTo (web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte:253-258) awaits load(); load() calls fetchGroups() with no cursor (:165, fetchGroups at :154-157 asks inbox.groups(filter, undefined, GROUP_ROWS)) and assigns list = l (:174), discarding groups appended by moreGroups (:205-214, appendGroups) and rows appended by more (:190-202, appendRows). soon() (:284) runs the same load() for a new unread item or an unlisted item changed elsewhere (:299) and on resync (:307). Groups per page default to DEFAULT_GROUPS (crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs:34). The header (InboxPage.svelte:18-19) promises a group keeps its place as its items are read here or elsewhere. Concrete user-visible failure before merge: blocker stands.","kind":"comment","references":"cb7873e276ea46cc594df7adc937b0e7a78e3cf233b0aad5f1354024d16083d0","summary":"confirmed: Mark read and every refetch replace the paged list with the first page of groups at default rows","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T00:10:19.183555Z","id":"d9578a1d25324b53daf022c452c850250589d7293e180f8164ee53387a8cc71b","body":{"detail":"toggleUnread sets filter.read = \"unread\" (web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte:248, unreadOnly at :104); markGroup -> markUpTo -> load() (:253-258, :265-268) refetches inbox.groups(filter, ...) (:155) with that filter, and inbox_groups builds the Groups shape from q (crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs:1617), so a group with no unread matches is not returned; list = l (InboxPage.svelte:174) removes it and the groups below shift up. The header (:18-19) says a group keeps its place until the search changes. Concern (owner's call on intended behavior) is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"435215598d6af7f50473d74747b527a140e69b4e80cdd00747c24b520974b3de","summary":"confirmed: with the Unread chip on, the post-mark refetch asks read=unread and the just-read group drops out","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T00:10:19.183714Z","id":"bfccf1498b269547f897aaf5727c8d6e5278dca26e3f28d5f34e129f37e46e78","body":{"detail":"web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte:345-346 places the Unread button inside div.filters#inbox-filters; :413-416 is @media (max-width: 700px) { .inbox .filters:not([data-open]) { display: none; } }, opened only by the Filters toggle at :343. The search box sits in .find (:341), outside it. Suggestion is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"915e999fcbf2d3b5a9bf324ac3021430acf018fa027fc0d26f2697f10399fdec","summary":"confirmed: the Unread chip lives in .filters, hidden at phone width until Filters is pressed","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T00:21:40.381157Z","id":"43daf4a1e2d0e815b976edc76b4caa71caecbc370ed240a0e653539a5b454bfb","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f17930430","summary":"Fixed: a mark and a live refetch now refresh: as many groups as are listed are fetched (limit = groups shown) and merged (inbox-groups.ts mergeGroups), each group keeping its place, its listed rows and its cursor. Evidence: inbox-page.test.ts 'keeps the groups paged in by More pages and the rows by Show more through a group's Mark read and a live refetch' (22 groups and a 5-row group kept through Mark read on a second-page group and a resync) passes in //web:unit.","supersedes":"cb7873e276ea46cc594df7adc937b0e7a78e3cf233b0aad5f1354024d16083d0","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T00:21:40.425594Z","id":"30f888fde9ecffe5bed45b8c43b64e61a17d427c84ec39fb844beb4f18800cb1","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:984b97851","summary":"Fixed by the approved one-list rule that a group's Mark read keeps it in place until the next load, applied under the Unread chip too: a group the refresh no longer lists there stays where it is, shown read, until the search or filter changes. Evidence: inbox-page.test.ts 'keeps a group read under the Unread chip where it is, shown read, until the next load' passes in //web:unit.","supersedes":"435215598d6af7f50473d74747b527a140e69b4e80cdd00747c24b520974b3de","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/InboxGroup.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T00:21:40.447965Z","id":"671e373c911e20193b8e53f20c48d0b1781627f5af0c6d7c7c89d789c59aaefe","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:234bebf6e","summary":"Fixed: while a group has something new its h3 is labelled 'Sales dashboard, 3 new', which names its toggle (aria-labelledby); the visible count is aria-hidden. Evidence: inbox-page.test.ts checks the heading's label and the hidden count; e2e/inbox.spec.ts finds the heading and the toggle by the exact name 'Sales dashboard, 5 new' in Chromium; both pass (f908f19f3, then 234bebf6e).","supersedes":"d15d01eec0c30b75f38307a100aeb9c2ce7f7d73c605aab655200c042c081741","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/QuestionCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T00:25:09.163947Z","id":"ec5ec18b4eb0f81cba4a00a7bfae2ff18f010ddd34364806c89eae313b833f29","body":{"detail":"With two or more questions the primary action reads 'Answer N more' until each has an answer and, pressed early, goes to the first unanswered one. With one question there is nowhere to go and 'Answer 1 more' reads oddly, so it stays 'Answer <agent>', disabled until answered, as before. Unit test: web/shell/src/q/question-card.test.ts 'answers every kind, saying how many are left'.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":295},"end":{"line":296},"content_hash":"2ff35f5c34f6c40b2e61f656806ca83a9963cb9823d6ecaf11285c8a740a9fad"},"summary":"A card with one question keeps a disabled 'Answer <agent>' rather than saying what is left","supersedes":"9857f68a7b3776244fa9ce4d379da9e2c79c13238939b00190d894d8017b98c3","tags":["revisit:a person reports a one-question card's disabled Answer as unclear","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/QuestionCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T00:25:09.269248Z","id":"bfcf1957341ccb96b0e3ee42adfe3b32477ea23b848ef8ba543c5d6e874c1077","body":{"detail":"The delay lets the person see the pick land (the radio and the tab's tick) before the next question replaces the options; another pick, a tab, Back/Next or typing Other in that time cancels the move. Moving at once would be faster for a person who reads ahead; the delay runs on the shell clock (web/shell/src/clock.ts after), so the e2e tests advance it.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":54},"end":{"line":55},"content_hash":"d0a60658d61b85d04e68d716b7d2e198c67ea5ade2c4886a8010c6595c6dee4e"},"summary":"A single choice's pick moves on after 250 ms, not at once","supersedes":"cf4b7d1f1dbedc1a59d4bbbe7390d3119013c61b0414e34b12fa5a5955aa30ff","tags":["revisit:the pause feels slow in use, or people re-pick during it","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T00:25:09.357138Z","id":"2c960f6169d6029521afbdd30cda77a0240659b8ae371f30c6dceb64928accf1","body":{"detail":"Moved from web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte:81, record 6c145291.\n\nloadStrip runs when the sections load and, debounced, on each inbox item change. An agent that starts, ends or renames without making an inbox item for this person (spec 2026-10-08 section 13: the agents topic announces those) shows in the strip only after the next inbox change or reload; block times tick on a 30 s clock.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":100},"end":{"line":100},"content_hash":"f1add4c6035f6d471f9604f2003769ef0f83030cee09058e7462a158afd034ad"},"suggested_fix":"Watch the person-scoped agents topic from the inbox page and refetch the strip on it.","summary":"The agent strip refreshes only with the inbox, not on the agents topic","supersedes":"4959a906562618c3b128c424c81fadf59fdc4432379b7693f9cdd552c7ba9a24","tags":["task:22","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T00:25:09.509600Z","id":"8d420fa647feb04aa7ae3599a51476ed4770abd374570fa2a343da47d6a1e0b7","body":{"detail":"The page fetches the unread question, approval and connection items (MAX_CARDS = 200) separately from the groups, and a group's rows and new count leave out exactly the items shown as cards. With more than 200 such items unread, the older ones are not cards: they show as rows in their page's group and count as new there. Before grouping, the flat unread list showed only its first page's cards too.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":146},"end":{"line":153},"content_hash":"c7fec710e98462a578cc37bea255eebdca8bd863e61a1ae640a8680238e30ace"},"summary":"Only the 200 newest unread card items show as cards; older open questions and requests fall into their groups as rows","supersedes":"a7d1a3455962b3c60a4c131c4cb7e8ffb317c89d84fcaa3f8370508afdcd59b6","tags":["inbox","shell","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T00:25:09.634017Z","id":"2e5c00489811f91423e1458945d737eee268e20a029000e44a236038780c4134","body":{"detail":"The Unread chip is inside .filters (InboxPage.svelte:345-346), which at max-width 700px is display:none until Filters is pressed (line 416). The one list's main narrowing control is thus two taps away on a phone, and whether it is on is not visible while the filters are closed.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":381},"end":{"line":382},"content_hash":"5f65c96e23bf7d291d3b59c71a2e2e89b69191d9daa61d836147546284a14fb6"},"suggested_fix":"Place the Unread chip in .find beside the search box (or show it outside .filters at phone width).","summary":"At phone width the Unread chip is hidden behind Filters","supersedes":"915e999fcbf2d3b5a9bf324ac3021430acf018fa027fc0d26f2697f10399fdec","tags":["review","review:inbox-one-list","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/inbox-groups.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T00:25:10.368540Z","id":"1a4ae75ceea5c8397328e01291e2648222294698a2755d39df2648cb0a36558a","body":{"detail":"Connection requests, machines that connected by invite, ended agents and questions asked outside a page have no artifact_id. They go in one group keyed `none` (the `artifact=none` filter of GET /api/inbox, crates/clax-server/src/routes/inbox.rs NO_ARTIFACT), ordered by its newest item like any page's group, titled \"Other\" with no link. A group per agent was considered: it would need a second grouping key in the store's GROUP BY (crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs Shape::Groups) and a way to page an agent's artifact-less items, and the agent strip already filters by agent. Connection requests, the most common of these items, are cards above the groups anyway.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":9},"end":{"line":33},"content_hash":"8122ef094ead38fd57ccd6c72c43225baab292f6b2ff82e07d7aa0c6d43a4068"},"summary":"Items about no artifact share one group, \"Other\", rather than a group per agent","supersedes":"af558a4d1d570e730e07cce1a5a63eeda88d8a3a4598dd8a5ffb79197f9575e1","tags":["inbox","shell","revisit:the Other group regularly holds more than a screenful of items from several agents","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T04:34:19.533733Z","id":"a30bc888cb37936341dfc8e0b8dbef5b58a72888edba784ac18dfb0f8ff6a496","body":{"detail":"listTags runs once on mount; a tag made, renamed or deleted while the inbox is open shows in the filter only after a reload. The inbox does not watch the gallery topic that carries the tags event.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":355},"end":{"line":355},"content_hash":"78f98086d42daa1644dde09e977b5631952cedf435ba76d4d15743ef297a1c19"},"summary":"The inbox's Tags filter lists the tags fetched when the page opened","tags":["tags","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:08:48.755030Z","id":"f2dff61bb4e33dab8795d5cb59ffb7fa7592ddcefa59274a9bc3b14607a0776f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:cfb4688dd","summary":"Fixed: InboxPage takes the page's stream (Gallery passes lm.pageStream()) and fetches the tag list again at each tags event with no artifact; tags.spec.ts 'the inbox's Tags filter…' renames q4 and sees the address become ?tag=design&tag=Q4+plan and the picker list Q4 plan checked (//web:e2e_rest tags.spec.ts inbox.spec.ts: 8 passed)","supersedes":"a30bc888cb37936341dfc8e0b8dbef5b58a72888edba784ac18dfb0f8ff6a496","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:11:01.842017Z","id":"0b90dc1100cef095b92d1bd7768ff31d1fbc7aef905e1a8c4baf35112677d3c3","body":{"detail":"Moved from web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte:81, record 6c145291.\n\nloadStrip runs when the sections load and, debounced, on each inbox item change. An agent that starts, ends or renames without making an inbox item for this person (spec 2026-10-08 section 13: the agents topic announces those) shows in the strip only after the next inbox change or reload; block times tick on a 30 s clock.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":109},"end":{"line":109},"content_hash":"f1add4c6035f6d471f9604f2003769ef0f83030cee09058e7462a158afd034ad"},"suggested_fix":"Watch the person-scoped agents topic from the inbox page and refetch the strip on it.","summary":"The agent strip refreshes only with the inbox, not on the agents topic","supersedes":"2c960f6169d6029521afbdd30cda77a0240659b8ae371f30c6dceb64928accf1","tags":["task:22","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:11:02.066329Z","id":"c4d7736ab6f6d556b82aa3eabe6531049f9cff54c7151cbd9ae95dcd9234ad8a","body":{"detail":"The page fetches the unread question, approval and connection items (MAX_CARDS = 200) separately from the groups, and a group's rows and new count leave out exactly the items shown as cards. With more than 200 such items unread, the older ones are not cards: they show as rows in their page's group and count as new there. Before grouping, the flat unread list showed only its first page's cards too.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":161},"end":{"line":168},"content_hash":"c7fec710e98462a578cc37bea255eebdca8bd863e61a1ae640a8680238e30ace"},"summary":"Only the 200 newest unread card items show as cards; older open questions and requests fall into their groups as rows","supersedes":"8d420fa647feb04aa7ae3599a51476ed4770abd374570fa2a343da47d6a1e0b7","tags":["inbox","shell","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:11:02.221693Z","id":"8693ee89fde67baa391406a8199473405ce0475943c6b47e1e5f287204545a9b","body":{"detail":"The Unread chip is inside .filters (InboxPage.svelte:345-346), which at max-width 700px is display:none until Filters is pressed (line 416). The one list's main narrowing control is thus two taps away on a phone, and whether it is on is not visible while the filters are closed.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":418},"end":{"line":419},"content_hash":"5f65c96e23bf7d291d3b59c71a2e2e89b69191d9daa61d836147546284a14fb6"},"suggested_fix":"Place the Unread chip in .find beside the search box (or show it outside .filters at phone width).","summary":"At phone width the Unread chip is hidden behind Filters","supersedes":"2e5c00489811f91423e1458945d737eee268e20a029000e44a236038780c4134","tags":["review","review:inbox-one-list","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/QuestionCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:09.909636Z","id":"717f473198e444bacd2703ecc874d694466edf2732932df1c168c525f5e90a3c","body":{"detail":"Only a question's text renders as Markdown; an option's label and description are text, as docs/contract.md's question shape says. A description sits inside the option's <label>, so a link in it would compete with picking the option, and it is part of the option's accessible name.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":269},"end":{"line":269},"content_hash":"6bf1150623a7bfb11e27dd83fe436fceefbed34c3def242643d8aa4e1c6b05e1"},"summary":"Render an option's description as Markdown too","supersedes":"96ef3e452ce200a2ce8bd6b4a4c324ba72ee0cb063a47b470da4bea79e053571","tags":["revisit:agents write Markdown syntax in option descriptions that shows literally","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/feed.svelte.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:09.964216Z","id":"9d2a17e001cd9d7c140f3c345a8662c1dd1ef8a5dd8d336a370a5a679c812ea3","body":{"detail":"InboxFeed.on (web/shell/src/q/feed.svelte.ts:281) sets `unread` from every event, and `summary()` sets it again from a GET started at `ready`, `resync`, `inbox_read` or SUMMARY_MS after an item change. A summary the daemon read before an item was made, whose answer lands after that item's event, puts the older count back until the next event or summary. QuestionFeed.refetch had the same shape and now replays the events heard while it was in flight; the inbox has no per-item list to replay into, so a fix needs the summary to carry a sequence (the inbox's newest `seq`) that the feed compares with the events'.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":234},"end":{"line":242},"content_hash":"e9e100bb7aedbf5ae9466ea2dfaa4dba4b2bedbda2c8d07085e99c7cf1dcb947"},"suggested_fix":"Return the newest inbox seq with the summary and with each event's unread, and keep the count from whichever is newer.","summary":"A summary read before an inbox event can overwrite the newer unread count that event carried","supersedes":"217cd397aaee94c94aa6c75a25404451582c7cb7d92754e8c0d57ccd84163454","tags":["race","shell","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/model.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:10.024341Z","id":"6cd16def86e60c9466d1d37139faa2541373d02268568c922cfd92e5967851c1","body":{"detail":"Sync::question marks a copy failed both at the backoff cap and when the remote refuses it (linked_question_failed with the remote's code and message, e.g. limit_reached past 8 open copies, record c759d6e6). questionLink ignores linked.error and always says unreachable, so a refusal from a reachable remote is misnamed. Retry lives only on the Publish popover's link row (failed_questions), while a thread card's not-sent line carries its own Retry (web/shell/src/view/linked-model.ts).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":111},"end":{"line":123},"content_hash":"b93615a87f23bbdf4aefaf2ec4f77f964418693ec7bb16c6da3a82845e9a849e"},"suggested_fix":"Word a refusal from linked.error (\"Not sent: refused by <remote>\") and give the card's not-sent line the same Retry a thread card has.","summary":"A question copy the remote refused reads 'Not sent: <remote> unreachable', and its card has no Retry of its own","supersedes":"39d62050ee9d45e667a05e4d39a57a9858a764f6d7fc8081fca0a38d3e383c78","tags":["review","ui","status:deferred","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/QuestionCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:47:45.189914Z","id":"0528e3f62bf9c118b6dd6171606d905a36bc20b991dfec77ea3ab8992321478e","body":{"detail":"With two or more questions the primary action reads 'Answer N more' until each has an answer and, pressed early, goes to the first unanswered one. With one question there is nowhere to go and 'Answer 1 more' reads oddly, so it stays 'Answer <agent>', disabled until answered, as before. Unit test: web/shell/src/q/question-card.test.ts 'answers every kind, saying how many are left'.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":297},"end":{"line":298},"content_hash":"ab697b92b4f0876d89ffc6dc7c65197415c553fed0cc53ff8bc4d6d71cd0872a"},"summary":"A card with one question keeps a disabled 'Answer <agent>' rather than saying what is left","supersedes":"ec5ec18b4eb0f81cba4a00a7bfae2ff18f010ddd34364806c89eae313b833f29","tags":["revisit:a person reports a one-question card's disabled Answer as unclear","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/feed.svelte.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T12:44:34.967182Z","id":"04a473bec5ba7ac06185afc6768400b08ae28a648084ad118e68baa113b5c3c8","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:c8b307ed1","summary":"Fixed in c8b307ed1 without a sequence on the wire: InboxFeed now takes a count from a request's answer (summary, page, groups, mark, markAll) only when no event carrying `unread` was heard since that request was sent (InboxFeed.counter). Every inbox change sends the topic an event with the count after it, so the latest heard event's count is never older than an answer read before it. Evidence: web/shell/src/q/feed.test.ts 'keeps the count of an event heard while a request was in flight, whose answer was read before that event's change' fails against the old feed.svelte.ts (expected [ +0, true ] to deeply equal [ 1, true ]) and passes with it (bazelisk test //web:unit --test_arg=shell/src/q/feed.test.ts: 12 passed). This race made ask-where.spec.ts:102 (dark, 1280) fail in CI run 40635079996 ('.topbar .inbox-link .count' not found at line 133); the spec with the first /api/inbox/summary answer held until the question showed fails the same way on the old feed (4/4) and passes with the fix (4/4).","supersedes":"9d2a17e001cd9d7c140f3c345a8662c1dd1ef8a5dd8d336a370a5a679c812ea3","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/RemoteRequestCard.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T03:16:44.133742Z","id":"66f8ea3b36cb7f870e31a6b38afef17b12a1d35655ef3df61f8915a22616daef","body":{"detail":"The request's inbox item carries the thread where_to_ask would place a question in (crates/clax-server/src/routes/remote_requests.rs ask; crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs note_remote_request), and the view gives it as item.thread. The shell renders the card on the inbox page alone (web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte decided snippet) and links 'in a thread'; the thread card's slots (web/shell/src/q/thread-slots.ts, ThreadQuestions.svelte) show questions only, so a person looking at the thread sees nothing there.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":63},"end":{"line":63},"content_hash":"0f8bcf8081aadfdd683bf08197602725b99bb74af4133b75b6d09615d4e5de9b"},"suggested_fix":"Give thread-slots a remote-request list from the inbox feed (kind remote_request, thread.id) beside ThreadQuestions, rendering RemoteRequestCard, as ThreadApproval does for approval requests.","summary":"A connection request placed in the asking agent's thread shows in the inbox with a link to that thread, not as a card inside the thread","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
