{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T08:56:23.115256Z","id":"6cf89b10265b6eb7ccb686a30645881a9222f468763714305e68989b33580566","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a5019f38","span":{"start":{"line":435},"end":{"line":435},"content_hash":"c87b0b6eca45577041b838900efb9fc8c0cf12d3b44c0a6e25123d4a33f10050"},"summary":"Only the owner's browser (the token is served) offers Connections, or a URL that already filters by it. Evidence: inbox-page.test.ts 'offers the Connections filter to the owner alone' passes; in Chromium Ivy's kinds list no Connections and the owner's do.","supersedes":"9c1b6fb05291bb483c9cb238d60c3dab64bc60db493c5cf7e69b29fef336bcf6","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T08:56:23.212842Z","id":"1b2cabe6bcd0217bb586a896a236207fc4ca5ed1cf29aee131d3b7258178a753","body":{"detail":"The Unread chip is inside .filters (InboxPage.svelte:345-346), which at max-width 700px is display:none until Filters is pressed (line 416). The one list's main narrowing control is thus two taps away on a phone, and whether it is on is not visible while the filters are closed.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":449},"end":{"line":450},"content_hash":"5f65c96e23bf7d291d3b59c71a2e2e89b69191d9daa61d836147546284a14fb6"},"suggested_fix":"Place the Unread chip in .find beside the search box (or show it outside .filters at phone width).","summary":"At phone width the Unread chip is hidden behind Filters","supersedes":"8693ee89fde67baa391406a8199473405ce0475943c6b47e1e5f287204545a9b","tags":["review","review:inbox-one-list","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/q/index.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T08:56:23.305141Z","id":"6bee189c79008539628df6b78f414824a8cc8165e3596a656db758b7c0cb89dd","body":{"detail":"artifact() mounts SidebarQuestions into the app's sheet (.app-questions > .questions-slot, slot() at line 100) instead of the hidden sidebar, but SidebarQuestions (web/shell/src/q/SidebarQuestions.svelte:19-30) shows only the questions in no thread as cards; a question in an open thread (inThread) appears there only as a ThreadLinks link (?thread=<id>) and counts in the heading, while its card, with the answer controls, is mounted by followSlots (line 125) into the thread card's .thread-q-slot in the sidebar, which app mode hides. The app is also told the question is open (count(), clax-questions), so its badge and openQuestions() lead to a sheet with nothing to answer. It comes from joining main's thread-card questions (a9c3a79a3c0b, 52d65826a74c) with the app-mode sheet (the commit 'Dock the shell's question card in app mode and tell the app how many questions are open'). Options: show thread questions as cards in the sheet in app mode (a flag to SidebarQuestions), or have the app's thread view mount the thread's .thread-q-slot.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":111},"end":{"line":137},"content_hash":"3af76e9e5f475d487953cfb5d96d13246cc938618fb51b407c252eec66c27031"},"summary":"In app mode a question placed in a thread can be answered only in that thread's card, inside the hidden sidebar","supersedes":"3e70286ad9abb42a2178771aeb8fd02bdbb2694016841391a8ec0d825eaa88db","tags":["app-mode","questions","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
